# ============================================================================
# .env.example — settings for scaler/compose.yaml
# ============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` in THIS folder (gitignored), then uncomment ONE model block
# and anything else you want to override. Compose auto-reads `.env` from the
# compose file's folder. From this folder:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose config    # preview the rendered command
#   docker compose up -d     # apply (recreates the container if it changed)
#
# Flag names live in compose.yaml's command, values come from here. With
# everything commented out, compose serves gpt-oss-20b on the B60's values.
#
# Switch a whole block, never single lines. Each block sets every
# model-specific variable, because carrying one across fails badly:
#   - VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS holds the flags only that model needs. gpt-oss's
#     --kv-cache-memory-bytes is absolute bytes for its weights; on a bigger
#     model the boot OOMs. Qwen3.8's --quantization sym_int4 is wrong for
#     gpt-oss, which ships pre-quantized.
#   - VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION: gpt-oss's byte value overrides it, so it
#     is only a fallback there. Qwen3.8 has no byte value and needs 0.90.
#   - A wrong reasoning or tool parser does not crash. You just get an empty
#     reasoning field or no tool_calls. After a switch, from the repo root:
#       MODEL=<served name> ./smoke.sh
# The served name changes with the block, so clients asking for one model's
# name stop working while the other runs.
#
# --enforce-eager is fixed in compose.yaml. Both blocks were measured with it,
# and gpt-oss returns empty output without it (./SCALER.md §4).
#
# One GPU: `docker compose down` in vllm_xpu/ or vllm_openai_xpu/ first.
# Details: ./SCALER.md "Models, and how to swap one".

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BLOCK A — gpt-oss-20b
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 12.87 GiB of weights, MXFP4 as shipped. 85.6 tok/s on the B60. The byte
# value was derived on the B60 for this image; not measured on the B70 yet.
# Re-derive it after an image change or on another card (./SCALER.md §3).
#
#VLLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
#VLLM_SERVED_MODEL_NAME=gpt-oss-20b
#VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=131072
#VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80
#VLLM_REASONING_PARSER=openai_gptoss
#VLLM_TOOL_CALL_PARSER=openai
#VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--kv-cache-memory-bytes 8647520256

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BLOCK B — Qwen3.8-27B, quantized to int4 as it loads
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The official BF16 checkpoint, quantized at load: 17.83 GiB on the card.
# Measured on the B70 only: 28.7 tok/s, smoke.sh ALL PASS. 128k needs 8.09 GiB
# of KV and util 0.80 left 4.13 GiB, so it runs 98,304 tokens at util 0.90
# (../INTEL_ARC_B70.md). vllm_openai_xpu/ runs this model faster and with the
# full 131,072: ../vllm_openai_xpu/QWEN3_8_27B.md.
#
#VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
#VLLM_SERVED_MODEL_NAME=qwen3.8-27b
#VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=98304
#VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.90
#VLLM_REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
#VLLM_TOOL_CALL_PARSER=qwen3_coder
#VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--quantization sym_int4 --dtype float16 --block-size 64 --mamba-ssm-cache-dtype float16

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MORE FLAGS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add a flag by appending it to your block's VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS, on one line
# separated by spaces. Put single quotes around a JSON value. Left unset,
# VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS is block A's byte value; set but empty, it adds nothing.
# Most obvious flags were already tried on this engine and rejected; read
# ./SCALER.md §4 and §8 first.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOST SETTINGS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Image. Leave it commented to follow the version this repo pins; a value here
# keeps you on it even after the repo moves on. Use an exact tag, never
# :latest (./SCALER.md §2). After an image change, re-derive block A's byte
# value (./SCALER.md §3).
#VLLM_IMAGE=intel/llm-scaler-vllm:0.26.0-b2
#
# Host port for the API. Without an address it listens on every interface.
# Put your host's LAN address in front to listen on that network only, e.g.
# 192.168.x.x:8000, and open the port to your subnet in the firewall. Clients
# on this host then need that address too, containers that use
# host.docker.internal included, and so do ./smoke.sh and ./bench.sh:
#   VLLM_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.x.x:8000 ./smoke.sh
#VLLM_HOST_PORT=8000
#
# What Docker does after a crash, a reboot or a Docker upgrade.
# unless-stopped brings this engine back on its own; "no" leaves it down until
# you start it, so a stopped engine can't fight another one for the GPU.
#VLLM_RESTART=unless-stopped
#
# GIDs of the host's render and video groups, which reach the GPU without
# root. They differ per host; check yours with: getent group render video
#RENDER_GID=992
#VIDEO_GID=44

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE THE MODELS LIVE (defaults = Docker's named volume, run as root)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To keep them in a folder you own, set BOTH lines below. Use the same values
# in every engine folder's .env, because the engines share the weights.

# Host folder for the weights. Must be an absolute path; `~` isn't expanded.
#HF_CACHE=/home/you/models/hf

# User the engine runs as: your `id -u`:`id -g`. The default 0:0 is root, so
# anything it downloads into your folder would be owned by root again. The
# GPU doesn't need root; group_add in compose.yaml passes render and video.
#VLLM_USER=1000:1000

# Hugging Face token for gated repos. Empty = anonymous. Neither block above
# is gated.
#HF_TOKEN=
